nfty ).$" 13194139535284 true] [17592186341634 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341635 13194139535284 true] [17592186341634 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341636 13194139535284 true] [17592186341634 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341637 13194139535284 true] [17592186341634 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341638 13194139535284 true] [17592186341634 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341639 13194139535284 true] [17592186341634 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535284 true] [17592186341634 1041 "selection" 13194139535284 true] [17592186341634 1104 #edb/ref 17592186341635 13194139535284 true] [17592186341634 1110 #uuid "a93e2f0d-a573-5a5d-9afa-f61b5baafbec" 13194139535284 true] [17592186341635 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535284 true] [17592186341635 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535284 true] [17592186341635 1111 #uuid "c735412a-f1ac-5bbf-ab67-f6928bd08cf3" 13194139535284 true] [17592186341636 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,1)" 13194139535284 true] [17592186341636 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535284 true] [17592186341636 1111 #uuid "9526e3a3-2617-5b33-917f-7f8cbb5b2700" 13194139535284 true] [17592186341637 1034 "x\\in (-2,2)" 13194139535284 true] [17592186341637 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535284 true] [17592186341637 1111 #uuid "97b167a7-e697-5a29-8bd3-b7cd480ac682" 13194139535284 true] [17592186341638 1034 "x\\in (-1,\\infty )" 13194139535284 true] [17592186341638 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535284 true] [17592186341638 1111 #uuid "8100a30b-463c-5508-9fab-fd71e18f5e65" 13194139535284 true] [17592186341639 1034 "x\\in (-1,1)" 13194139535284 true] [17592186341639 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535284 true] [17592186341639 1111 #uuid "11df97b8-5f77-5c77-ab73-96e00961510c" 13194139535284 true] [17592186341640 1017 #edb/ref 17592186341641 13194139535284 true] [17592186341640 1089 "q-125292" 13194139535284 true] [17592186341640 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535284 true] [17592186341640 1100 "Find the interval of convergence for the series\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{n}}{{2}^{n}(3n-1)}=\\frac{x}{2\\cdot 2}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{2}\\cdot 5}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{2}^{3}\\cdot 8}+⋯\\,.\n$$" 13194139535284 true] [17592186341640 1113 #uuid "b88949dc-1e89-5760-9055-7f75b5d5164e" 13194139535284 true] [17592186341640 1145 "To apply the ratio test, we define ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{x}^{n}}{{2}^{n}(3n-1)}.$ Then, we calculate the ratio of two successive terms and take the limit as $n\\to \\infty :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{x}^{n+1}}{{2}^{n+1}(3n+2)}\\cdot \\frac{{2}^{n}(3n-1)}{{x}^{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{x(3n-1)}{2(3n+2)}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|x|}{2}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{3n-1}{3n+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{|x|}{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{|x|}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe series converges if $L<1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{|x|}{2}<1\\,⟹\\,|x|<2.\n$$\n\nSo, the radius of convergence is $2,$ and the series converges for any $x$ that lies in the open interval $(-2,2).$\n\nThe ratio test gives no conclusion about the convergence of the series when $L=1.$ So, when $|x|=2,$ we do not know if the series converges. This means that the endpoints $x=-2$ and $x=2$ need to be investigated separately using another test for convergence.\n\n- When $x=2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{n}}{{2}^{n}(3n-1)} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{2}^{n}}{{2}^{n}(3n-1)} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{3n-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{1}{8}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo see if this series converges, we use the limit comparision test, whith ${a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{3n-1}$ and ${b}_{n}=\\frac{1}{n}.$ We observe that ${a}_{n}$ and ${b}_{n}$ are positive, and\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{{a}_{n}}{{b}_{n}}={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{1}{3n-1})}{(\\frac{1}{n})}={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{n}{3n-1}=\\frac{1}{3},\n$$\n\n \nwhich is positive and finite. Hence, the series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ and ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ either *both* converge or *both* diverge.\nSince ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{n}$ is divergent, the series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{3n-1}$ is also divergent by the limit comparison test. So the endpoint $x=2$ is not included in our interval.\n\n- When $x=-2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{n}}{{2}^{n}(3n-1)} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-2)^{n}}{{2}^{n}(3n-1)} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{3n-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{5}-\\frac{1}{8}+⋯,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is convergent by the alternating series test. So the endpoint $x=-2$ is included in our interval.\n\nTherefore, the interval of convergence is $[-2,2).$" 13194139535284 true] [17592186341641 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341642 13194139535284 true] [17592186341641 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341643 13194139535284 true] [17592186341641 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341644 13194139535284 true] [17592186341641 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341645 13194139535284 true] [17592186341641 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341646 13194139535284 true] [17592186341641 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535284 true] [17592186341641 1041 "selection" 13194139535284 true] [17592186341641 1104 #edb/ref 17592186341646 13194139535284 true] [17592186341641 1110 #uuid "1e6cb124-653f-56c6-aee0-f17d3a7d164e" 13194139535284 true] [17592186341642 1034 "x\\in [-2,2]" 13194139535284 true] [17592186341642 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535284 true] [17592186341642 1111 #uuid "f2d89c84-9ed6-584a-987d-0b414840ae3d" 13194139535284 true] [17592186341643 1034 "x\\in (-4,4]" 13194139535284 true] [17592186341643 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535284 true] [17592186341643 1111 #uuid "8b65f225-e7a1-5e62-855a-2e15f88f728d" 13194139535284 true] [17592186341644 1034 "x\\in (-2,2)" 13194139535284 true] [17592186341644 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535284 true] [17592186341644 1111 #uuid "41ec57c3-26fd-5cf1-a5af-76b16c4d7c92" 1319